# Specialist routing (Job Finder)

When a task clearly belongs to a Job Finder specialist, prefer that subagent over general-purpose. Wiring metadata lives in `.cursor/agent-system/registry.json` — do not duplicate full agent prompts here.

**Default:** Job Finder feature/plan/integration work → `conductor` (“Use the conductor to plan and route this work”).

## Defaults

| Need | Agent | Notes |
|------|-------|-------|
| Plan, parallel waves, integrate, roadmap | `conductor` | Does not implement features |
| Docs, constitution, contracts, design system prose | `jobfinder-agent` | Wave A peer with database |
| Vite SPA / inbox UI | `jobfinder-frontend` | Wave B |
| Collectors / Actions schedule | `jobfinder-discovery` | Wave B; public ATS only |
| Migrations / RLS / PostgREST exposure | `jobfinder-database` | Wave A; never wipe pgrst list; no pgvector |
| `job-ingest` Edge Function | `jobfinder-ingest` | Wave B |
| Structured résumé / tailor drafts / provenance | `jobfinder-resume-writer` | Owns `src/lib/resume/` + tailor EF |
| Fit ratings / independent ATS audit rubrics | `jobfinder-fit` | Legacy/frozen catalog `score.ts` + YAML; **not** product ranking |
| Gatekeeper sole product scorer | `jobfinder-gatekeeper` | Luna (`gpt-5.6-luna`); JWT score + batch worker; persist `gatekeeper_*`; never sync ingest hot path |
| Guided apply / propose fills / browser helper | `jobfinder-apply` | Never clicks Submit; human-in-the-loop |
| Verify / build / browser | `jobfinder-tester` | Wave C; before “done” |
| Create a new agent | follow `scale/AGENT_CREATION.md` | via `create-agent.mdc` |

## Invoke

Use each agent's registered phrases from the registry (also under **Invoke phrases** in the spec).

## Lifecycle

Every Job Finder specialist report must end with:

```text
**Lifecycle:** memory=unchanged|changed | promotion=none|<what> | dashboard=clean|refresh-required | handoff=none|<sibling|conductor>
```

